  "articleBody": "Installing door casings might seem like a simple DIY, but there are some common blunders that can quickly turn your project into a headache. One of the biggest mistakes is poor measurement; cutting the pieces too short or too long means visible gaps or an ill-fitting frame, and nobody wants that! Another frequent issue is leaving visible gaps from bad miter cuts or uneven walls. You really need to take your time to get those angles right, and if your walls aren't perfect, a pro knows how to handle those irregularities for a seamless look. Failing to anchor the casing securely is another common pitfall. If it's not fastened well, it can shift, leading to cracks or looseness down the road. And finally, always, always check that the door frame stays plumb and square *before* you finish up. If the frame gets knocked out of alignment during installation, your door won't operate smoothly. When walls are out of square, or you need to match existing millwork perfectly, that's when a professional, like us at HH Remodeling LLC, really shines. We make sure your door casings are installed beautifully and correctly the first time, serving folks across the Denver metro area and beyond.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
